WEBVTT

00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:01.711
The first website ever.

00:00:01.723 --> 00:00:02.971
What was it about?

00:00:02.981 --> 00:00:04.393
Comment your answer.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.918
Tim Berners-Lee ran it at CERN, on

00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:09.803
this NeXT computer, the first web server.

00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:12.186
It explained the web itself, the brand

00:00:12.196 --> 00:00:13.867
new World Wide Web.

00:00:13.877 --> 00:00:16.894
Berners-Lee had come up with the web

00:00:16.904 --> 00:00:18.306
at CERN in 1989.

00:00:18.406 --> 00:00:22.030
And it's still online, at info.cern.ch.
